It turns out that HP does publish a binary platform compatibility
statement. It is very good news.

Here is the link. Thanks to those who helped and responded.

http://h30097.www3.hp.com/pdf/5.1b_1_binary_compatibility2.pdf=20

-----Original Message-----
From: Siebert, Aaron=20
Sent: Monday, September 19, 2005 10:43 AM
To: 'tru64-unix-managers-owner@ornl.gov'
Subject: 5.1a versus 5.1b

Managers,

I have been tasked with analyzing the differences of 5.1a and 5.1b. The
goal being to understand the software differences between the 2 versions
of platforms in hope of delivering software compiled on 5.1a but
delivered to run on 5.1b. We are missing some required libraries to
compile on 5.1b.

Here is what I can think that would be useful if anyone has any
